          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तिराहा — tirāhā — \"a T-junction, a meeting of three roads\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तिराहे से बाएँ मुड़िए। tirāhe se bāẽ muṛiye. Turn left at the T-junction."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तिराहा (tirāhā) is the three-way partner of चौराहा: ti-, \"three\", as in तिकोना, with rāh, \"road\", usually traced to Persian rāh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
