        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चक्कर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चक्कर — cakkar — \"a round; a detour; dizziness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ग़लत रास्ते की वजह से हमें लंबा चक्कर लगाना पड़ा। ġalat rāste kī vajah se hamẽ lambā cakkar lagānā paṛā. Because of the wrong road we had to go a long way round."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चक्कर (cakkar) आना, to feel dizzy: मुझे चक्कर (cakkar) आ रहा है."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चक्कर (cakkar) is a semi-learned form of Sanskrit cakra, \"a wheel, a circle\" (CDIAL 4538); the fully inherited Hindi form in that entry is cāk, \"a wheel, a millstone\". A चक्कर is any going round: a detour, a round of the market, a spinning head."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
